{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron","id":1265351,"title":"What Exactly Is Cold Iron?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-07T12:17:54-08:00","id":1265351,"title":"What Exactly Is Cold Iron?","content":"From the way it's described in fantasy, &quot;Cold Iron&quot; appears to be a special method of forging iron, or might refer to something that is made out of pure iron, instead of being mixed into an alloy of some kind.<br /> <br /> But when I try to look up cold iron forging methods, or even what classifies as cold iron, the internet only gives me an indication that &quot;cold&quot; iron is just another name iron in general. It can also be referred to as &quot;Cold Steel&quot; in some cases.<br /> <br /> So I'm really confused by this, especially when it comes to a Changeling game. I specifically need to know two important pieces of information regarding the game and its setting.<br /> <br /> 1 - What is Cold Iron?<br /> <br /> 2 - How common is Cold Iron in the modern world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T13:20:28-08:00","id":1265366,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell cold iron is iron that wasn't made in a blast furnace, at least from the C20 description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blast_furnace\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Alto_Horno%2C_Puerto_de_Sagunto%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-04%2C_DD_91.JPG/960px-Alto_Horno%2C_Puerto_de_Sagunto%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-04%2C_DD_91.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blast_furnace\" target=\"_blank\"> Blast furnace - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blast_furnace\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blast_furnace </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cold iron isn't very common now, used to be most common form. Blast furnaces started being used in Europe in the 15th century, and by the 19th century was pretty much the only method of manufacture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T14:09:41-08:00","id":1265377,"title":"","content":"Cold iron is a poetic term in the same way cold steel is used in literature so sayeth this Wikipedia article: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore</a><br /> <br /> Common objects that are mostly iron:<br /> Cast iron cooking implements (not the aluminum ones)<br /> Drain pipes in many areas of the US<br /> Fireplace tools<br /> Forging tools<br /> Metal grill and range tops<br /> <br /> In older houses:<br /> Lamp frames<br /> Furniture frames<br /> Window clasps<br /> Door handles and hinges<br /> Most hand tools<br /> Horseshoes<br /> Actual iron irons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T15:03:28-08:00","id":1265388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron?p=1265377#post1265377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold iron is a poetic term in the same way cold steel is used in literature so sayeth this Wikipedia article: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_in_folklore</a><br /> <br /> Common objects that are mostly iron:<br /> Cast iron cooking implements (not the aluminum ones)<br /> Drain pipes in many areas of the US<br /> Fireplace tools<br /> Forging tools<br /> Metal grill and range tops<br /> <br /> In older houses:<br /> Lamp frames<br /> Furniture frames<br /> Window clasps<br /> Door handles and hinges<br /> Most hand tools<br /> Horseshoes<br /> Actual iron irons</div> </div> </div> </div>In Changeling though it's more specific than that.<br /> <br /> P. 291 C20 &quot;Cold iron is not what most humans think of as iron...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T18:06:02-08:00","id":1265415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron?p=1265388#post1265388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Changeling though it's more specific than that.<br /> <br /> P. 291 C20 &quot;Cold iron is not what most humans think of as iron...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, it's iron that's been heated over a charcoal flame. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T08:17:04-08:00","id":1265511,"title":"","content":"I would also say that cold iron tends to be older things. Iron that was imbued with the coldness of the era- railroad ties or old fences or other things that are emblematic of the industrial era that put machines ahead of man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T15:56:50-08:00","id":1265608,"title":"","content":"Unrelated I count meteroic iron as Always cold iron even if alloyed or well forged becuase space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T16:50:48-08:00","id":1265617,"title":"","content":"Odd. Wrought iron isn't considered brittle and it's the iron used in anvils and the Eiffel tower. Charcoal is not commonly used now and the puddling process is used to make wrought iron. There goes my idea of my mages dealing with changelings in pan to pan combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T17:01:29-08:00","id":1265618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron?p=1265617#post1265617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd. Wrought iron isn't considered brittle and it's the iron used in anvils and the Eiffel tower. Charcoal is not commonly used now and the puddling process is used to make wrought iron. There goes my idea of my mages dealing with changelings in pan to pan combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> drop meteors on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T20:28:09-08:00","id":1265662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron?p=1265618#post1265618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> drop meteors on them</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll make the same ruling regarding your head canon. Although it seems like a rock from the sky that can be fashioned into a sword seems pretty awe inspiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T01:29:52-08:00","id":1265726,"title":"","content":"Personally I think meteors are so much closer to, and likelier to generate, Glamour than Banality and as such any metal taken from a meteor would much more likely be Glamour infused than anything considered Cold Iron. After all meteoric metals and weapons forged from them are the stuff of legends.<br /> <br /> I believe Cold Iron is meant to be the earliest type of wrought iron, the so called charcoal iron, that in the past depending upon the skill and experience of the smith was of varied quality. If the charcoal content was left too high it was brittle and a sword made of it would shatter on a hard blow while another time when worked to a lesser charcoal content it would be more durable and much more fitting for weaponry. But in general yes wrought iron is rather durable form of iron, it\u2019s famous uses mentioned above. But like said I believe it is meant that puddling process that replaced charcoal iron at the dawn of the industrial age doesnt produce Cold Iron as meant in Changeling. I could be wrong though so YMMV. And still well made charcoal iron is extremely durable, resistant to corrosion and definately not brittle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Typo 11-09-2018, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T04:09:24-08:00","id":1265755,"title":"","content":"I would have meteoric iron be a material that does aggravated damage to Changelings, but is not infused with Banality. That's totally a house rule thing though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:27:47-08:00","id":1265974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1265351-what-exactly-is-cold-iron?p=1265662#post1265662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'll make the same ruling regarding your head canon. Although it seems like a rock from the sky that can be fashioned into a sword seems pretty awe inspiring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think of it as manifest banality but abit like soulsteel in Exalted. It burns changelings and eats their soul. Why? Because its from beyond the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T01:20:50-08:00","id":1266124,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the point of this is that traditionally-forged iron was the first 'mundane' metal. Before we learned to work with iron, metal that we could make stuff with was fairly rare and special, but when we started finding and using iron we suddenly had plenty. Thus metalwork became banal and that banality still persists in traditionally forged iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T11:57:02-08:00","id":1266242,"title":"","content":"Personally, I houserule that anything made with malicious intent is cold iron. Weapons have a lot of singular-usage themes -- to kill -- but the <i>reasons </i>they're made can be myriad from &quot;I'm commissioned to do this&quot; to &quot;I need to defend myself and my family&quot; to &quot;my liege lord gave me this as a symbol of his trust in me&quot;. Anything forged in pure &quot;I need to destroy my enemy&quot; would count as cold iron. <br /> <br /> That's just me though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}